    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> alexcrichton submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14416#pullrequestreview-5319465234\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Could this perhaps be something where a <code>task_group_hook.rs</code> submodule could be made to help split out code and reduce the <code>#[cfg]</code> traffic in <code>concurrent.rs</code>? (also in the spirit of keeping the file a bit smaller...)</p>\n<p>Also, would it make sense to revert other work from #13510 such as the <code>FuncCallConcurrent</code> abstraction? (as that's sort of no longer relevant)<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 626925886,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790350760
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14416#discussion_r4106003939\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>In addition to having the method here, can the method also be on <code>StoreContextMut</code>?</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 626925887,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790350760
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> alexcrichton created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14416#discussion_r4106116716\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Would it be possible to integrate this into <code>GuestTask::new</code> and perhaps <code>HostTask::new</code>?</p>\n<p>I'm a bit wary to sprinkle incref/decref throughout the code in various locations because it feels like inevitably we'll forget to put one somewhere. By handling it once on construction and once on destruction however that feels more natural to me.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 626925888,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1790350761
